scope one keystone -- the placement of a contained fault, generalized from one guard to a named class and proven on the second instance
status GREEN -- conflict_marker witness green on metal, 50 readings over 19 planted states in 19 real repositories, including the two that arm the real pre-commit hook; census and list output byte-identical over 17,266 tracked files; exec_bit ok, no mode drifted. The cold open read 236 guards, 230 green, 4 red, tree_moved=no, head_behind_anointed=0. Of those four, one is standing_equipment reporting that a rostered guard reddened, and index_row_bound is repaired in this lap. The two that stand are count-pins off by one and are named on the card rather than loosened.
recommend check-in (Keaton) -- two things want your word and neither is agent-doable: the REDS bound, which has now blocked four ships' rows in one day, and whether tame_reach's ceiling should be retired rather than raised a third time.
